# heavy-gate max load: the 5-minute load average above which no new heavy job starts. One number above 0 on a line of its own; fractions are fine.
#
# No number here means 12 (this Mac has 8 cores). Load gates a start only: it never stops or slows a job that is already running.
# A value that is 0 or not a number is ignored (the default 12 applies, with a warning).
# The file is read on every try, so an edit reaches jobs that are already waiting (on this version of heavy-gate).
# HEAVY_GATE_MAX_LOAD=N in a job's environment overrides this file for that one job.
#
# Edit by hand. Every start also passes the memory and disk rules; those are not set here.
# chezmoi creates this file only if it is absent and never overwrites it: your edits stay.
